Etapa 5: the status window showed a critical of 128 or more as negative.
The server sends Critical as 0..255 (handler/item.go refreshScore clamps
it to 255; protocol/score.go writes it as a u8) and every combat use in
the runtime reads it as (unsigned char), but the decompiled status
window read the signed char: 190 (76.0%) printed as "-26.-4%".

diff --git a/Projects/TMProject/TMFieldScene.cpp b/Projects/TMProject/TMFieldScene.cpp
--- a/Projects/TMProject/TMFieldScene.cpp
+++ b/Projects/TMProject/TMFieldScene.cpp
@@ -13962,7 +13962,7 @@
 		sprintf(szStr, "%d%%", nAttSpeedValue);
 		if (m_pAttackSpeed)
 			m_pAttackSpeed->SetText(szStr, 0);
-		int nCriticalValue = pMobData->Critical;
+		int nCriticalValue = (unsigned char)pMobData->Critical;
 		nCriticalValue *= 4;
 
 		sprintf(szStr, "%d.%d%%", nCriticalValue / 10, nCriticalValue % 10);
